"                                    <br/><br/>Here Filters means any Filters visible on List/Tree view.\n"
"                                    <br/><br/>Group By means any Group By visible on List/Tree view."
msgstr ""

#. module: simplify_access_management
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:simplify_access_management.access_management_form_view_ah
msgid ""
"You can hide access of action buttons, object buttons, tabs and links (in kanban box) of any model for specified user from this tab.\n"
"                                    <br/><br/>Here Button means any action button visible on any view.\n"
"                                    <br/><br/>Page means any tab visible on any form view.\n"
"                                    <br/><br/>And Link means any action link visible on Kanban view.\n"
"                                    <br/><br/>More Info :"
msgstr ""

#. module: simplify_access_management
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:simplify_access_management.access_management_form_view_ah
msgid ""
"You can set strict access rights of the model(read, write, delete, update) and set the domain to access the model's records for any user and from one place. The access defined here will either allow or block the entire access from the specified user(s), not only from the system, but also from the code and API. So be careful while defining the accesses here. If you just want to hide the Create, Edit and Delete buttons from the backend user for sales order but want to allow them to use POS, then defining access here will genereate the error on POS side. To prevent that, you can use the 'Model Access' tab to Hide the Create, Edit and Delete buttons.\n"
"                                    <br/><br/>You can allow the Read (View), Write (Create), Delete, Update (Edit) rights by just checking the check-boxes of respective actions, and to restrict them of those rights, don't check any of those checkboxes. And also this tab gives you advance configurator to allow those rights for your user on specific conditions, to set that condition check 'Apply Filter' checkbox.\n"
"                                    <br/><br/>More Info :"
msgstr ""

